{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And they encamped in the wilderness of Paran.</b> In a place within the wilderness that had no name at all, but was opposite Kadesh-barnea and close to it, in order to arrange their affairs and enter there — for it is the first city of the land of Israel that they reached on that journey, as he testified in saying (Deuteronomy 1:19–21): וַנָּבֹא עַד קָדֵשׁ בַּרְנֵעַ, and says: אֲלֵיכֶם בָּאתֶם עַד הַר הָאֱמֹרִי אֲשֶׁר ה׳ אֱלֹהֵינוּ נֹתֵן לָנוּ, עֲלֵה רֵשׁ וגו'. And that place was called Rithmah, as explained in these journeys (Numbers 33:18)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:34.638805019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}